1. Docker Container Keeps Restarting ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐
Interviewer:

"Your Docker container is restarting continuously. How do you troubleshoot?"

Possible Causes
Application crash
Missing environment variables
Wrong startup command
Database connection failure

Commands
docker ps -a
docker logs <container-id>
docker inspect <container-id>

Example
Exited (1)

Restarting...
Sample Answer

I first check the container logs using docker logs to identify the application error. Then I verify the Dockerfile, startup command, environment variables, mounted volumes, and database connectivity.


2. Container Exits Immediately ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐
Interviewer
"Container starts and exits immediately."

Reason
Main process completed.

Example
CMD ["echo","Hello"]

Output
Hello
Container Exited
Because Docker expects one foreground process.

Fix
Run the actual application.


